{"name":"Venus Pink","hex":"#f0e5e5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"venus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the bivalve molluscs in the genus Venus or family Veneridae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/venus"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Venus","blocks":[{"text":"Venus is the second planet from the Sun. Similar in size and mass to Earth, Venus has no liquid water, and its atmosphere is far thicker and denser than that of any other rocky body in the Solar System. The atmosphere is composed mostly of carbon dioxide and has a thick cloud layer of sulfuric acid that spans the whole planet. At the mean surface level, the atmosphere reaches a temperature of 737 K, making it the hottest planet in the solar system and also a pressure 92 times greater than Earth's at sea level, turning the lowest layer of the atmosphere into a supercritical fluid. From Earth, Venus is visible as a star-like point of light, appearing brighter than any other natural point of light in the sky, as either the brightest \"morning star\" or \"evening star\". It was also given the poetic name Ēarendel in Old English, meaning \"ray of light\" along with the two previous epithets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Venus_from_Mariner_10.jpg/330px-Venus_from_Mariner_10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Terrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png/500px-Terrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Terrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png/500px-Terrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATerrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/11214_2023_956_Fig3_HTML.webp/500px-11214_2023_956_Fig3_HTML.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/11214_2023_956_Fig3_HTML.webp/1280px-11214_2023_956_Fig3_HTML.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/11214_2023_956_Fig3_HTML.webp/500px-11214_2023_956_Fig3_HTML.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Venus imaged in different wavelengths","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A11214_2023_956_Fig3_HTML.webp"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Venus_globe.jpg/500px-Venus_globe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Venus_globe.jpg/1280px-Venus_globe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikime